@startuml Webhook Processing System with Smart-Contract Integration

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Webhook Processing System - Smart-Contract Integration\n(Hybrid Pattern with Contract Awareness)

actor "Payment\nProvider" as Provider
participant "WebhookController" as WC #FFE082
participant "EventDispatcher" as ED #C5E1A5
participant "WebhookHandler" as WH #FFF3E0
participant "ContractRepository" as CR #F8BBD0
participant "PaymentCaptureHandler" as PCH #FFF3E0
participant "OrderRepository" as OR #E1F5FE
participant "PaymentService" as PS #FFF9C4
database "osc_payment_contract" as ContractDB #FFE0B2
database "oxorder" as OrderDB #B2DFDB

== Webhook Received from Provider ==

Provider -> WC : POST /webhook\n+ signature header\n+ payload (providerOrderId, status)
activate WC

note right of WC
  **Webhook Controller Responsibilities:**
  1. Verify webhook signature (security)
  2. Parse webhook payload
  3. Emit domain event (event-driven)

  **NO business logic here!**
end note

WC -> WC : Verify webhook signature\n(HMAC-SHA256 / RSA)

alt Signature Invalid
  WC --> Provider : 401 Unauthorized\n{"error": "Invalid signature"}
  note right
    Security: Reject invalid webhooks
    Prevents spoofing attacks
  end note
else Signature Valid
  WC -> WC : Parse JSON payload:\n{\n  "providerOrderId": "ord_123",\n  "transactionId": "txn_456",\n  "status": "COMPLETED"\n}

  WC -> ED : **Emit** PaymentCapturedEvent(payload)
  activate ED

  note right of ED
    **Event-Driven Pattern:**
    Webhook emits event,
    handlers react
  end note

  ED -> WH : handle(PaymentCapturedEvent)
  activate WH

  == Phase 1: Identify Contract via Provider Order ID ==

  note right of WH
    **Smart-Contract Integration:**

    OLD: Find oxorder by provider ID
    NEW: Find contract first,
         contract knows order ID
  end note

  WH -> WH : Extract providerOrderId\nfrom webhook payload

  WH -> CR : findByProviderOrderId(providerOrderId)
  activate CR

  CR -> ContractDB : SELECT * FROM osc_payment_contract\nWHERE OXPROVIDERORDERID = 'ord_123'
  activate ContractDB

  note right of ContractDB
    **Contract Record:**
    {
      "OXID": "contract123",
      "OXSTATE": "COMMITTED",
      "OXORDERID": "order789", ← Has order!
      "OXPROVIDERORDERID": "ord_123",
      "OXPROVIDER": "stripe"
    }
  end note

  ContractDB --> CR : Contract data
  deactivate ContractDB

  CR --> WH : PaymentContract\n{orderId: "order789"}
  deactivate CR

  note right of WH
    **Benefit of Contract:**

    • Single lookup finds both
      contract and order ID
    • Contract tracks provider ID
    • Clean separation of concerns
  end note

  == Phase 2: Verify Contract State ==

  WH -> WH : Verify contract state:\n• contract.getState() == COMMITTED?\n• contract.getOrderId() != null?

  alt Contract Not Committed
    note right of WH
      **Error Handling:**
      Contract must be in COMMITTED
      state to process payment capture
    end note

    WH -> WH : Log error: "Contract not committed"
    WH --> ED : Handler complete (error)
    deactivate WH
    ED --> WC : Event processed
    deactivate ED
    WC --> Provider : 200 OK\n(acknowledge, but no action)
    deactivate WC

  else Contract Is Committed

    == Phase 3: Load Order via Contract ==

    WH -> OR : find(contract.getOrderId())
    activate OR

    OR -> OrderDB : SELECT * FROM oxorder\nWHERE OXID = 'order789'
    activate OrderDB

    OrderDB --> OR : Order data
    deactivate OrderDB

    OR --> WH : Order\n{id: "order789",\n status: "NOT_FINISHED"}
    deactivate OR

    == Phase 4: Validate Payment Data ==

    WH -> WH : Extract transactionId\nfrom webhook payload

    WH -> PS : fetchPaymentDetails(providerOrderId)
    activate PS

    note right of PS
      **Double-Check Payment:**
      Query provider API to verify
      webhook data integrity
    end note

    PS -> Provider : GET /payments/{providerOrderId}
    activate Provider

    Provider --> PS : Payment details:\n{\n  "status": "captured",\n  "amount": 99.99,\n  "currency": "EUR"\n}
    deactivate Provider

    PS --> WH : PaymentDetails
    deactivate PS

    WH -> WH : Validate:\n• Amount matches order\n• Currency matches\n• Status is successful

    alt Validation Failed
      WH -> WH : Log error: "Payment mismatch"
      WH --> ED : Handler complete (error)
      deactivate WH
      ED --> WC : Event processed
      deactivate ED
      WC --> Provider : 200 OK\n(acknowledge, investigate)
      deactivate WC

    else Validation Passed

      == Phase 5: Update Transaction ==

      WH -> OrderDB : INSERT INTO osc_payment_transaction\n(OXORDERID, OXPROVIDERORDERID,\n OXTRANSACTIONID, OXTYPE, OXSTATUS,\n OXAMOUNT, OXCURRENCY)\nVALUES ('order789', 'ord_123',\n 'txn_456', 'capture', 'completed',\n 99.99, 'EUR')
      activate OrderDB

      note right of OrderDB
        **Transaction Record Created:**

        Links:
        • Contract (via provider order ID)
        • Order (via order ID)
        • Provider (via transaction ID)
      end note

      OrderDB --> WH : Transaction saved
      deactivate OrderDB

      == Phase 6: Emit Contract Fulfillment Event ==

      WH -> ED : **Emit** ContractPaymentCapturedEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
      activate ED

      note right of ED
        **Event Chain:**
        ContractPaymentCapturedEvent
        triggers contract fulfillment
      end note

      ED -> PCH : handle(ContractPaymentCapturedEvent)
      activate PCH

      == Phase 7: Fulfill Contract ==

      PCH -> CR : find(contractId)
      activate CR

      CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
      activate ContractDB
      ContractDB --> CR : Contract
      deactivate ContractDB

      CR --> PCH : PaymentContract
      deactivate CR

      PCH -> PCH : contract.fulfill()

      note right of PCH
        **Contract Fulfillment:**

        State: COMMITTED → FULFILLED

        Contract lifecycle complete:
        ✓ Created (intent)
        ✓ Conditions met
        ✓ Order created
        ✓ Payment captured
        ✓ Fulfilled
      end note

      PCH -> CR : save(contract)
      activate CR

      CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE osc_payment_contract\nSET OXSTATE = 'FULFILLED',\n    OXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()
      activate ContractDB

      note right of ContractDB
        **Final Contract State:**
        {
          "OXSTATE": "FULFILLED", ✓
          "OXORDERID": "order789",
          "OXFULFILLEDAT": "2025-10-20..."
        }
      end note

      ContractDB --> CR : Updated
      deactivate ContractDB

      CR --> PCH : Saved
      deactivate CR

      == Phase 8: Finalize Order ==

      PCH -> OrderDB : UPDATE oxorder\nSET oxpaid = NOW(),\n    oxtransstatus = 'OK',\n    oxfolder = 'ORDERFOLDER_NEW'
      activate OrderDB

      note right of OrderDB
        **Order Finalized:**

        State: NOT_FINISHED → OK

        Now ready for:
        • Fulfillment/shipping
        • Invoice generation
        • Customer notification
      end note

      OrderDB --> PCH : Order updated
      deactivate OrderDB

      == Phase 9: Trigger Side Effects ==

      PCH -> ED : **Emit** ContractFulfilledEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
      activate ED

      note right of ED
        **Multiple Subscribers React:**

        1. EmailSubscriber
           → Send order confirmation

        2. InventorySubscriber
           → Update stock levels

        3. AnalyticsSubscriber
           → Track conversion

        4. AuditLogSubscriber
           → Log completion

        5. InvoiceSubscriber
           → Generate invoice
      end note

      ED -> ED : Notify all subscribers:\n• EmailSubscriber.sendConfirmation()\n• InventorySubscriber.updateStock()\n• AnalyticsSubscriber.trackConversion()\n• AuditLogSubscriber.logCompletion()

      ED --> PCH : All subscribers notified
      deactivate ED

      PCH --> ED : Handler complete
      deactivate PCH

      ED --> WH : Event chain complete
      deactivate ED

      WH --> WC : Handler complete (success)
      deactivate WH

      WC --> Provider : 200 OK\n{"status": "processed"}
      deactivate WC

    end
  end
end

note over Provider, OrderDB
  **Smart-Contract Webhook Benefits:**

  ✅ **Single Lookup**: Contract found by provider order ID,
     contains order ID - no separate query needed

  ✅ **State Validation**: Verify contract is COMMITTED
     before processing capture

  ✅ **Complete Audit Trail**: Contract tracks full lifecycle
     from intent to fulfillment

  ✅ **Clean Separation**: Webhook updates contract first,
     then order - clear ownership

  ✅ **Event-Driven**: Multiple subscribers react to
     ContractFulfilledEvent automatically

  ✅ **Idempotency**: Webhook can be replayed - contract
     state prevents duplicate processing
end note

note over Provider, OrderDB
  **Idempotency Handling:**

  If webhook is delivered multiple times (common):

  1. Find contract by provider order ID ✓
  2. Check contract.getState()
     • If already FULFILLED → Return 200 (already processed)
     • If COMMITTED → Process capture
  3. State machine prevents duplicate fulfillment

  **Result:** Safe webhook redelivery without side effects
end note

note over Provider, OrderDB
  **Error Scenarios Handled:**

  1. **Contract Not Found:**
     → Log error, return 200, investigate
     → May indicate provider sent webhook before contract created

  2. **Contract Wrong State:**
     → Return 200, log warning
     → Contract may be CANCELLED or EXPIRED

  3. **Payment Validation Failed:**
     → Return 200, create alert
     → Amount/currency mismatch requires investigation

  4. **Order Not Found:**
     → Critical error, log + alert
     → Contract has orderID but order doesn't exist (data corruption)
end note

@enduml
